Tuesday
Today we were able to meet up again with Setsuko! We showed up at the park
to talk and play Ground Golf and she showed up with a fresh haircut. She
cuts her hair with scissors herself using two mirrors to see the back, shes
awesome. She said we were both cute with our haircuts too. Before we played
she recalled some of her memories she had of her two younger and very
naughty brothers. When they were kids, their mom got a phone call from the
school that the sons went too, and apparently one of them had broken all
the windows Of the school =F0=9F=98=88=F0=9F=92=80 one of them also sprayed=
 a fire extinguisher
Off of the top floor. That's a whole new level of rambunctious. The
funniest story she told us (in her opinion) was when one of her brothers
was 4 years old, he jumped straight into a pond trying to catch a butterfly
with his net. Setsuko acted this out with a big jump which definitely
surprised me considering she's 75 (I think). She also has arthritis so I
don't really know how she's moving around so well, she's super energetic
and I'm all here for it. We also got to exchange Line with her, so now we
have a solid contact method!! We didn't get to talk much about gospel stuff
but It was a good chance to get to know her and her background better.
Afterwards we did Some housing and I used the flower method
=F0=9F=8C=B8=F0=9F=8C=BB=F0=9F=8C=B9=F0=9F=8F=B5=F0=9F=8C=B7=F0=9F=A5=80=F0=
=9F=8C=BC=F0=9F=8C=BA=F0=9F=92=A0=F0=9F=92=90 Basically we ting the doorbel=
l at the house of someone
with a lot of pretty flowers or something and I'll ask if it's OK for me to
take a picture of them. Today we tried it and got to talk with some lady in
her front yard for a solid 5-10 minutes! She showed us all her different
flowers and their names, and we even talked a bit about our missions. We
invited her to Eikaiwa and it seems like she had a little bit of interest,
she's practiced English by listening to the radio before! Hopefully we get
to meet her again!

We visited art store lady again! I need to get her name memorized, I heard
it once but totally forgot. She was pretty busy helping a guy get some art
stuff for a news broadcast (crazy) but she saw we had an interest in
calligraphy and tried to help us get set up with some free classes with
some random teacher. I also picked out some watercolor paper to try, and
when she saw me trying to look for more coins to pay for it, she grabbed my
hand and took only the money I had (it was less than the paper) and sent me
out of the store with my paper =F0=9F=98=AD=F0=9F=98=8A shes so sweet but I=
 literally want to
like support the store. We will definitely visit again! We had Eikaiwa
today, and before it started 2 random people (I think past students from
like years ago) showed Up and wanted to say hi to us for a little while. We
talked a bit about church stuff and a bit about Eikaiwa but it was super
random. The two were maybe a couple (not sure) but they were for certain
previously dance partners =F0=9F=92=83=F0=9F=95=BAThey were in their 70=E2=
=80=99s and weren't able to
stay for long but it was nice to meet them. We played ping pong before
Eikaiwa with one lady and she and I went back and forth for like 100 pings
and tongs without missing a hit. It was like the spirit of ping pong was so
strong =F0=9F=91=BB Eikaiwa was fun, afterwards Shiko showed us his acousti=
c-electric
guitar. It was super cool, and it blows my mind just how light they are
compared to electric guitars lol. Today Setsuko also sent us a bunch of
voice memos which are so cute and always in English. She told one of her
friends about me and Magbago=E9=95=B7=E8=80=81 and she wants to meet with u=
s! From what
Setsuko said she doesn't have much Of a gospel interest maybe, but Setsuko
would like to talk about our beliefs all together with her. This will
happen in 2 weeks, let's go!

Today we had exchanges with the Gobo elders, and I can say with surety that
Gobo is the most Inaka (countryside) part of the mission. There's hardly
anyone there. I was partnered up with Downs=E9=95=B7=E8=80=81 and like 10 P=
ercent of the
doors we knocked even answered. One guy answered in a towel and had just
gotten out of the bath. There was no reason he had to answer the door like
that but it was awesome, props to him. Me and Matsuhisa=E9=95=B7=E8=80=81 a=
lso played some
Pok=C3=A9mon that night, and the game was like 2 hours long =F0=9F=98=B1 I =
ended up losing
but I also chose not to just kill him in the first couple rounds so I feel
validated. He also gave me much praise for my Japanese speaking, as a
native he thinks I'm like cracked at Japanese. It's a very sweet sentiment,
especially from another missionary who has likely seen all kinds of other
missionaries and their own levels of Japanese. God has really blessed Me
with an increased ability to speak and listen in Japanese as I have tried
to align my will to His.

Today we had 3 Jimoty pickups, and because my comp don't got money ATM we
biked to meet up with the 3 people. One of them was a bunch of assorted
tools for 200=C2=A5, one of them was a couple guitar pickups for 1000=C2=A5=
, and
another was a pair of 4kilogram exercise weights. Can you guess which one
we picked up first?? The weights =F0=9F=92=80 Can you guess How far we bike=
d today?
30 Miles =F0=9F=92=80=F0=9F=92=80=F0=9F=92=80 The whole time I carried arou=
nd those weights and it was
wild. Not sure I've biked a longer distance in one day In my whole life.
Also having the weights made it significantly tougher. We crossed 4 cities
in between meeting with all of those people. As usual we invited them all
to our Eikaiwa classes and I left them positive reviews on Jimoty. It was
crazy for real. I also got real crisped up From the sun, I will attach a
picture. While biking home we tried to visit a house I=E2=80=99d been attem=
pting to
knock at least twice before. This time they answered the doorbell but
immediately said no thanks even while I was saying how I loved their disney
themed fence. Tragic. We also tried to say hi to a member by the church and
she answered but we didn't exactly bring anything for her and she didn't
have time for a longer visit so we gave a bit of an awkward greeting and
left lol.

Sunday Surprise
At church we had a recently baptized member named Daniel show up to
Sacrament meeting. He's been living in Japan for around 8 months and he's
from Paraguay. We are hopefully gonna hang out with him on Pday! He lives
pretty far and travels by bike so he hasn't gotten to attend church before
now Since coming to Japan. What=E2=80=99s crazy is that he was tought and i=
nvited
to baptism by a Sister Killian =F0=9F=98=AE Here's something crazy. A day b=
efore we
met Daniel, a sister missionary named Dossett=E5=A7=89=E5=A6=B9 =E2=99=A5=
=EF=B8=8F sent me a Facebook
profile for an Elder Kade Killian who was called to serve in Japan 3 ish
years ago. We met Daniel and it was Elder Kade Killians sister who served
in Paraguay and taught Daniel about the gospel. Insane divine inspiration
from Dossett=E5=A7=89=E5=A6=B9. Today me and Magbago played one of the card=
 games he like
called Union Arena And it was pretty fun.

Random Missed note from last week, during exchanges met a high-school Girl
on her porch and talked a bunch about Religion and what eternal life
sounded like to her, and she even said that she imagines it would be living
forever married =F0=9F=91=80

Pday was miserably rainy, weren't able to hang out with Daniel cause of it.
we did bike a little ways to get groceries though. I bought a foot pedal
thingy for my guitar and another CD. Not at the grocery store if that
wasn't apparent Lol. We have plans to meet with Jiro tonight, I'll have to
talk about how it goes next week =F0=9F=98=81 (it went well, I'm writing th=
is late
and after we met with him. We Invited him to meet up with the missionaries
in Australia And he seems like he's excited to!)

Spiritual thought
This week has been a week of huge progress as a companionship. Getting out
and doing Missionary work feels so good. Things aren't perfect, and there's
definitely times where we aren't using our Time 100 percent perfectly but
it's way better than it has been. I can promise to each of you reading this
that no matter what difficulties you are facing, God knows your trials and
struggles. I have really tried to see things from his perspective recently,
Maybe holding my tongue against my companion or waking him up if I don't
want to =F0=9F=98=82 (not happening all that often Fortunately) or followin=
g a
prompting from the spirit. Things really seem much better as you are
striving to Follow God's plan. It's different in each of our lives, so I'd
invite you to pray and sincerely ask God what His plan looks like for you.
Maybe even ask what you can do. I'm sure you'll be surprised by the
response you get, I definitely have been.

I love each and every one of you! I'm grateful to be serving the Lord. I
hope that my email can be a light to some one of my friends out there =F0=
=9F=98=81

Elder Killian

